{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     custom-about.hbs — a page that opens with a hero.
     Shape from NSDS templates/personal-site.html.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     A Ghost custom template: make a page, pick "About" in the editor. It is
     named for its use rather than its shape because that is what the
     dropdown shows an author, but nothing here is about-specific — sponsor,
     become-an-author and any other page that should open with a statement
     rather than a heading can use it.

     ── WHY NOT JUST page.hbs ───────────────────────────────────────────────
     page.hbs is deliberately plain: title, optional cover, prose. That is
     right for a policy page and wrong for the one page whose job is to make
     a case. The difference is the hero — full-bleed, dark, gridded — which
     page.hbs cannot grow without growing it for every page.

     ── show_title_and_feature_image IS STILL HONOURED ──────────────────────
     gscan fails a page template that ignores it, and rightly: the switch is
     in the editor either way, so ignoring it makes the editor lie. Here it
     controls the WHOLE hero rather than a title, because on this template
     the title IS the hero — an author who turns it off has written their own
     opening into the body and must not get a second one above it.

     The hero is data-driven throughout: no headline, no strapline and no
     image is a valid page, and each simply does not draw. A hard-coded
     headline here would be the ⚠ DUMMY problem that partials/home/ still
     carries in two bands.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#post}}
{{#if @page.show_title_and_feature_image}}
    <section class="ns-band ns-hero ns-band--dark ns-band--grid">
        <div class="ns-band__inner">
            <div class="ns-band__head">
                <h1 class="ns-band__title">{{title}}</h1>
                {{#if custom_excerpt}}<p class="ns-band__lede">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>{{/if}}
            </div>
            {{#if feature_image}}
                <img class="ns-card__media" src="{{img_url feature_image size="xl"}}"
                     srcset="{{img_url feature_image size="l"}} 1000w, {{img_url feature_image size="xl"}} 2000w"
                     sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 1200px, 100vw"
                     alt="{{#if feature_image_alt}}{{feature_image_alt}}{{/if}}">
            {{/if}}
        </div>
    </section>
{{/if}}

<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        {{!-- gh-content AND ns-prose, both — see page.hbs for the long
             version. Without .gh-content, Ghost's own cards.min.css wins and
             every card is a white box on the navy surface. --}}
        <div class="gh-content ns-prose">{{content}}</div>
    </div>
</section>
{{/post}}
